    "done_when": "One fetch entry point in nova/database/layer_fetch.py runs oras blob fetch against ghcr.io/iterorganization/efitpp-test-data by layer digest, verifies the sha256 and publishes the blob through the content store, using its public publish and verified-read functions rather than its internal helpers; tests/data-manifest.json gains entries for the analytic pair and the CORSICA 130506, DINA 105027 and ASTRA 131046 input and reference layers, each with its full layer digest re-derived from the registry manifest (the plan text truncates them and they must not be transcribed), its per-dataset dd_version and its case metadata, and the mutable tag appears nowhere in code; tests/test_layer_fetch.py proves a correct fetch of the analytic layer, refusal when one manifest digest is altered, and a clean skip when the registry is unreachable; tests/test_transport_geometry_reference.py, which reads the same manifest, still passes; logs in the manifest",
